  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#unhandled-promise-rejections\r\n\r\n> If notHandled is false, then the promise rejection is handled\\. Otherwise, the promise rejection is not handled\\.\r\n> \r\n> If p's \\[\\[PromiseIsHandled\\]\\] internal slot is false, add p to settings object's outstanding rejected promises weak set\\. \r\n\r\nShould the second line instead be this?\r\n\r\n>  If notHandled is false, add p to settings object's outstanding rejected promises weak set\r\n\r\nIt's unclear to me why we are checking `notHandled` in the previous step and then `PromiseIsHandled` in the next step. It seems like, as currently written, `notHandled` doesn't have any effect. (It's possible I'm just misunderstanding, so please feel free to point that out.)\r\n",
